 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Where to look:** `make_signer` (`src/tessel/sessions.py:303-321`) builds the serializer from `SECRET_KEY_HISTORY` plus the current `SECRET_KEY`. Cookies signed with the old key only validate if that old key is in `SECRET_KEY_HISTORY`. You most likely replaced `SECRET_KEY` without adding the old value there, so every existing cookie failed signature verification and users were logged out.\n\n**How to rotate without logout:**\n\n1. Set the new key as `SECRET_KEY`.\n2. Put the old key(s) in `SECRET_KEY_HISTORY` (a list), e.g. `SECRET_KEY_HISTORY=[old_key]`.\n3. Deploy. Old cookies still verify and get re-signed with the new key on the next response.\n4. After your session lifetime has passed (`PERMANENT_SESSION_LIFETIME`), remove the old key from the history.\n\n**Things to check:**\n- Make sure every instance gets both settings at the same time. A mix of old and new configs will cause intermittent logouts.\n- The history key must match the old key byte for byte (str vs bytes encoding, whitespace from env vars).\n- Anything else that uses `SECRET_KEY` directly, such as extensions, CSRF tokens, or signed URLs, may not honor the history (`docs/config.rst:140`). Those could still break.\n- `salt`, `digest_method` and `key_derivation` must stay unchanged, or old cookies won't verify either.",
